From f5d047135abd53800aa3cc1a241f9bd22922d5d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lineage-build <build@localhost>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:08:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Updater: Label incremental updates as incremental

Every installable entry said "Full install: Safe to install over any
previous build", including incremental packages, which apply only
over the one build they were made from.

Carry the source build of an incremental in the update: from the
feed (files[0].pre_build_incremental) or, for an imported package,
from its metadata precondition. Label such entries as incremental,
and block one whose source is not the installed build instead of
letting update_engine fail at the source hash check.

Drop feed entries that are incrementals for another build, and the
full OTA of a build that an applicable incremental reaches, so one
feed listing every incremental serves every build. A feed keyed on
the running build can't: builds that were never published had no
feed file, and their update check failed with HTTP 404.

Change-Id: I209c8636a6e5dc3272806f73f56b4bdf7077ad72
